course: dictionary
lesson: 14845
title: Rainstorm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rainstorm is a storm with heavy rain, often with strong wind. You may already know the two small words inside it: rain and storm. Rain falls from clouds, and a storm is a time of rough weather. Put them together and you get the meaning. «The rainstorm hit the town at lunchtime, and the streets were soon full of water.» The words heavy and full of water are the clues.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Strong wind bent the trees as the rainstorm rolled in.» The wind tells you this is a storm, not just a light shower. Try your meaning in the sentence: a storm with heavy rain and strong wind fits perfectly, so you can trust it.
explain: Rainstorms can cause floods, so weather and geography lessons study them. «When the rainstorm ended, the river had risen over the bridge.» That is why safety matters: during a rainstorm, stay indoors and keep away from rivers and flooded roads.
fact: A rainstorm is a storm with heavy rain, often with strong wind.
fact: Rainstorm is made of two smaller words you already know: rain and storm.
fact: Rainstorms can cause floods, so they are studied in weather and geography lessons.
fact: Safety: in a rainstorm, stay indoors and keep away from rivers and flooded roads.
fact: Rainstorm is a noun: one rainstorm, two rainstorms.
exercise: «The rainstorm turned the village road into a river.» What is a rainstorm? | A dry wind that blows over the desert | A quiet, gentle snowfall | *A storm with heavy rain, often with strong wind | A bright, sunny day at the beach
exercise: «We stayed inside while the rainstorm passed.» Where should you be during a rainstorm? | Walking along a flooded road to get home | *Indoors, away from rivers and flooded roads | Standing under a tall tree | Out on the riverbank to watch the water
exercise: Which two smaller words make up rainstorm? | *rain and storm | rain and stone | rainbow and snow | run and storm
test: «Heavy rain and strong wind battered the coast all night in the rainstorm.» What does rainstorm mean? | A cold, clear morning | *A storm with heavy rain, often with strong wind | A quiet, dry night | A small sprinkle of drizzle
test: Why did Ben's class study rainstorms in geography? | Because they only happen in summer | Because they are a type of cloud | Because they make the sun shine brighter | *Because they can cause floods
exam: Which is the best safety rule during a rainstorm? | Walk through flooded roads to get home quickly | Climb a tall tree to see better | Go down to the river to watch the water | *Stay indoors and keep away from rivers and flooded roads
